#![enable(implicit_some)]
// Sample library for building the UI before import and generation exist.
// Loaded by `src/model/sample.rs`. Facts are named by `key`, and résumés cite
// them by key. A résumé is a list of sections:
//
//   Header(contacts: [keys])                 the name, then these contact facts
//   Summary(line)                            a paragraph
//   Experience / Projects / Education([(entry: "key", bullets: [lines])])
//                                            each entry with its title,
//                                            organization, dates, location and
//                                            stack, then the bullets chosen
//   Skills([(group: "key", only: [skills])]) a skill group, all of it unless
//                                            `only` picks some
//   List(title: …, items: [lines])           a titled list outside any entry
//
// and a line is one of:
//
//   Fact("key")                        the fact's text, citing it
//   Reworded(text: …, cites: [keys])   generated wording that differs from the facts
//   Edited(fact: "key", text: …)       generated as the fact's text, then edited by the user
//
// `template` picks the résumé's template, from `typeset::TEMPLATES`.
//
// Every fact's text (or `source`, when extraction mangled it) must appear
// verbatim in its document: `from`, or its entry's, or "cv". An entry's facts
// are looked for after its title. `also_in` lists other documents a fact was
// found in, as if duplicates had been merged. `edited` is the user's
// rewording. Résumés are generated from the facts as extracted and not
// hidden, so edits and hiding came after.
//
// The data covers every state the facts screen shows: unreviewed, confirmed,
// hidden, flagged, edited, merged from two documents, a likely duplicate,
// facts from notes, and facts changed after a résumé used them.
(
    documents: [
        (key: "cv", kind: File("alex_rahman_cv.pdf"), text_file: "cv.txt", added_days_ago: 12),
        (key: "linkedin", kind: File("linkedin_profile.pdf"), text_file: "linkedin.txt", added_days_ago: 5),
        (
            key: "fest_note", kind: Note, added_days_ago: 2,
            text: "Organizer, Code Fest 2019, University of Dhaka Programming Club\nRan a volunteer team of 15 students over the three days.\nFound sponsors who covered the whole budget.",
